om VP_03 by then. So fine. VP_02 pad: M01 arrival 24, turnaround 25. VP_02 pad at 24: arrival, 25: turnaround. VP_05 pad M07: depart 27, travel 27, arrival 27, turnaround 28. So VP_05 pad 27 arrival, 28 turnaround. All good.\n\nNow, we need to check charging for UAV_03 M02 with charge_blocks=1: charging at VP_07 after M02 turnaround (9) in slot 10. Does slot 10 have charger capacity? VP_07 charger capacity 2. UAV_03 uses one charger slot. No other charging. So ok. Also, check battery upper bound after charging: UAV_03 battery capacity 22.0. SOC after charging = initial 2.731181 - 0.1359 + 0.95 = 3.545281, well below 22. So ok.\n\nNow, a possible issue: corridor capacity for COR_11 with UAV_02 M05 using it at slots 8,9. COR_11 capacity default 2, so fine. But the intervention also has capacity override at slot 7 only (1). So slot 8,9 unaffected. So ok.\n\nBut check M05 departure at 8: COR_11 travel 8-9, need to check wind: COR_11 wind level 0 according to path PATH_04. UAV_02 max wind level 1, so ok. M02 path PATH_08 (COR_07) wind level 0, UAV_03 max wind level 2, ok. M03 path PATH_12 wind level 1, max 2 ok.\n\nNow, we must also verify that UAV_02 M05 departure 8 does not violate release window? Release is 7, due 9. So earliest depart 7, we depart 8, that's after release, fine. Due 9, but due is typically deadline for arrival? Since travel 2 slots, departure 8, arrival 9, meets due 9 exactly. So no tardiness.\n\nNow, about the lexicographic objective: we want to minimize total holds. So no holds is optimal (0 holds). Next, repair distance? Not sure what \"repair distance\" means. Maybe total distance flown of repaired missions? So sum of distances of all served missions. Baseline total distance: M01 1.0, M02 1.2 (but now we change), M03 0.8, M04 2.55, M05 1.06, M06 1.0 (PATH_06? baseline used PATH_06 1.0, but we will use PATH_09 1.0 also), M07 0.75. So sum = 1.0+1.2+0.8+2.55+1.06+1.0+0.75 = 8.36? But we will change M02 distance to 0.9, M06 distance to 1.0 (same), M05